---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Shell from '../../components/shell/Shell.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/shell/PageHead.astro';
import Explain from '../../components/shell/Explain.astro';
---
<Base title="Deployment | SKUdesk" description="How SKUdesk runs on Google Cloud, with live checks."><Shell>
<PageHead title="Deployment" sub="How it runs on Google Cloud, with live checks."/>
<Explain>
A Node service on <b>Cloud Run</b>, a <b>Firestore</b> database, a <b>Cloud Scheduler</b> job and <b>Secret Manager</b> for keys, with <b>Gemini</b> reading each listing's text and photo. The state below is read from the running service when you open the page.
</Explain>
<section class="card" aria-labelledby="c-h"><h2 id="c-h">Services</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Used for</th><th>State</th></tr></thead><tbody id="parts"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="card" aria-labelledby="q-h"><h2 id="q-h">Search budget</h2><div class="split" id="bar" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="muted sm" id="q-note"></p></section>
<section class="card" aria-labelledby="s-h"><h2 id="s-h">Security headers (read from this page's own response)</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Header</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody id="sec"></tbody></table></div>
<ul class="steps-list">
<li>Scripts only from this origin; no inline script runs. Listing text is untrusted and only ever set as text.</li>
<li>Product images pass through an allow-listed proxy, so the page cannot be used as an open proxy.</li>
<li>Rate limits per caller, a cap on concurrent checks, a monthly search budget and a body size limit.</li>
<li>Owner controls need a key; approvals need the requester's token or the owner key.</li>
<li>Secrets live in Secret Manager. The service account can only reach this service's database.</li>
</ul></section>
</Shell></Base>
<script>
  import { api, h, int, when } from '../../lib/client.ts';
  const pill = (c: string, t: string) => h('span', { class: `pill ${c}` }, t);
  Promise.all([api('/health').then(() => true).catch(() => false), api('/api/status'), api('/api/scans').catch(() => []), api('/api/merchant/status').catch(() => ({ configured: false })), fetch('/', { method: 'HEAD' })]).then(([healthy, st, scans, ms, page]) => {
    const last = scans[0]?.createdAt;
    const fs = String(st.store).startsWith('firestore');
    const rows: [string, string, HTMLElement][] = [
      ['Cloud Run', 'API and the site, deployed from source', pill(healthy ? 'good' : 'bad', healthy ? 'live' : 'down')],
      ['Firestore', 'Cache, checks, proposals, history, audit log', pill(fs ? 'good' : 'warn', fs ? 'live' : 'local file')],
      ['Cloud Scheduler', 'Scheduled scan of the watchlist', last ? pill('good', `last scan ${when(last)}`) : pill('warn', 'no scan yet')],
      ['Secret Manager', 'Gemini, SerpApi, Merchant, owner and scan keys', pill('good', 'in use')],
      ['Gemini', 'Identity gate, photo check, retail recall, grounded note', pill('good', 'live')],
      ['Google Shopping via SerpApi', 'Listings and prices', pill('good', 'live')],
      ['eBay Browse API', 'A second source of listings', st.sources.ebay ? pill('good', 'live') : pill('', 'joins when its key is added')],
      ['Google Merchant Center', 'Resale listings for approved buys', ms.connected ? pill('good', 'live') : ms.configured ? pill('warn', 'needs attention') : pill('', 'ready to connect')],
      ['Seller checkout', "Approval records the decision and opens the seller's link", pill('ok', 'by design')],
    ];
    document.getElementById('parts')!.replaceChildren(...rows.map(([a, b, c]) => h('tr', {}, h('td', {}, a), h('td', { class: 'muted' }, b), h('td', {}, c))));
    const fill = h('i', { class: 'a' }); fill.style.width = `${Math.min(100, (st.quota.used / st.quota.limit) * 100)}%`;
    document.getElementById('bar')!.replaceChildren(fill);
    document.getElementById('q-note')!.textContent = `${int(st.quota.used)} of ${int(st.quota.limit)} searches used this month. Every search is cached for 12 hours, so repeats are free.`;
    const keys = ['content-security-policy', 'strict-transport-security', 'x-frame-options', 'x-content-type-options', 'referrer-policy', 'permissions-policy', 'cross-origin-opener-policy', 'cross-origin-resource-policy'];
    document.getElementById('sec')!.replaceChildren(...keys.map((k) => h('tr', {}, h('td', { class: 'mono xs' }, k), h('td', { class: 'mono xs muted', style: 'overflow-wrap:anywhere' }, page.headers.get(k) ?? 'not set'))));
  }).catch(() => {});
</script>
<style>.steps-list{margin:var(--s4) 0 0;padding-left:20px;display:grid;gap:var(--s2);color:var(--mut)}</style>
